{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`CodeReviewBatchRunner.run` iterates only the static `req.criteria` list and stamps each finding\nwith `reviewer_id = prompt_id` and no logical criterion id\n(`src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py:49,79`). The code-review gate YAML injects only the 13\nbuilt-in overlays (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/code-review.yaml:77-94,109-126`), so an activated\nproject criterion never enters Round A/B and, even if it did, its findings could not be attributed\nto `project.<name>`. Plan-review already solves the related dynamic-membership problem at runtime\n(`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:206-225`). Code review differs because its\nsingle runner serves both `round_a` and `round_b`; project fan-in must therefore be explicitly\nonce-only. This is the second of five seams (root cause on superseded bug 8a4b).\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a Round-A-only project-criteria input to the existing code-review runner:\n\n- At the code-review batch assembly point in `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` (where\n  `CodeReviewBatchRunner` is constructed around `gate_dispatch.py:643-645` and `repo_root` is\n  available as `request.repo_root`), read `registry.effective_criteria(repo_root)` plus\n  `registry.effective_routing(repo_root)`. Select active `project.` ids whose routing entry has\n  `exec: LLM`; DET-tier project criteria remain outside this LLM finder path. Resolve each physical\n  prompt with `criterion_prompt_id(cid, gate_key=\"code_review\")`\n  `[rebar:fc72-bf7e-7652-4228]` and build entries carrying both `prompt` and logical `criterion_id`.\n- Extend `CodeReviewBatchRunner.__init__` with an additive default-empty `project_criteria` tuple.\n  `run()` combines `req.criteria` with those entries only when `req.step_id == \"round_a\"`; for\n  `round_b` it uses only `req.criteria`. The runner instance may therefore serve both YAML batch\n  steps without double execution. Activated project criteria are deliberately once-per-review\n  opt-ins rather than recommendation/glob-driven built-ins, so they run in Round A and do not\n  consume or bypass the Round-B escalation cap of three. No seen-set or cross-run mutable state is\n  used, keeping retries/replays deterministic.\n- When a project entry emits findings, preserve any model-emitted `criteria` tags and append the\n  logical `criterion_id` once if absent; keep the existing physical `reviewer_id` provenance.\n- If an activated project criterion prompt is missing or malformed, fail loudly with a located\n  `LLMError` naming the logical criterion and expected\n  `.rebar/prompts/<physical-prompt-id>.md` path. Errors reading or validating\n  `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` are not swallowed or degraded to built-ins: the shared criteria\n  loader error propagates, so invalid project configuration cannot silently disable review.\n\n**Rejected alternatives.** Adding static project slots to `code-review.yaml` cannot work because\nproject ids are repository-specific. Appending project entries to every `BatchRunRequest` would\nexecute them in both rounds. A mutable seen-set would make retries and replay depend on call order.\nThe Round-A-only branch on the stable YAML step id is explicit, stateless, and testable.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` — assemble active LLM project entries and pass them to\n  the runner.\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py` — accept project entries; inject them in Round A\n  only; append logical criteria ids; raise a located prompt error.\n- `tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py` — extend the shared file; add a synthetic repo\n  fixture that activates `project.foo` and writes\n  `.rebar/prompts/code-review-project-foo.md`, reused by later children.\n\n`BatchRunRequest`, the workflow interpreter, YAML membership, Pass-3 routing, and the Round-B cap\nare unchanged. Pass-3 project posture is owned by dependent child 58ef.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path plus workflow boundary (`fan_in`): run the real two-round workflow with a stub finder;\n  `project.foo` executes exactly once in `round_a`, never in `round_b`, and every emitted finding\n  retains existing tags plus logical id `project.foo`.\n- Direct runner edge: invoking a `round_b` request with project entries configured does not append\n  or execute them; replaying a `round_a` request produces the same once-per-call plan without\n  retained mutable state.\n- Parity: an overlay-absent repo produces the same ordered built-in Round-A/Round-B requests and\n  findings as before; no project entries are present.\n- Config error (`missing`): active `project.foo` with no prompt raises a located `LLMError` naming\n  both `project.foo` and `.rebar/prompts/code-review-project-foo.md`.\n\nTier: unit plus an offline workflow integration using the real interpreter and stubbed agent calls.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] An activated LLM-tier project criterion executes exactly once across the complete Round-A +\n      Round-B workflow, in Round A, and each finding preserves prior tags while carrying logical\n      `project.<name>`; verified by\n      `rtk .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k fan_in`.\n- [ ] An overlay-absent repo yields the unchanged ordered built-in batches and findings; verified by\n      `rtk .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k parity`.\n- [ ] A project criterion with a missing prompt raises a located `LLMError` naming the criterion and\n      expected path; verified by\n      `rtk .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k missing`."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1784920534969696001,"uuid":"7e22f9d3-9df8-49c8-b15a-390152dda20d"}